    <statement><p>An object moves along a straight track from the point
<m>(-4, -2, -3)</m> to the point <m>(-6, -10, 7)</m>.  The only
force acting on it is a constant
<m>\mathbf F = -4 {\mathbf i} + 4 {\mathbf j}  - 3 {\mathbf k}</m> newtons.
Find the work done if the distance is measured in meters.</p>
<p>Work = <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> joules.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-54</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
